{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the surgical team members. You're here because of worsening dry heaves and trouble keeping food down. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, thank you. It started a few weeks ago—just a few dry heaves a week. But now it’s several times a day. I can’t eat much without feeling like I’m going to heave again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And any vomiting with actual content, or just dry heaves?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Just dry heaves. No vomiting. Bowel movements are normal—no blood or black stools."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, good to know. You had a gastric bypass years ago, and then a G-tube placed, which was removed recently—is that right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I had the G-tube for nutrition, but I asked to have it removed. Since then, the pain and heaving got worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. Your history shows you’ve had ulcers at the surgical site before. We’re concerned that might be flaring up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could that be causing the dry heaves?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, irritation or an ulcer in the stomach remnant can cause nausea and retching, even without vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to start you on IV fluids to keep you hydrated and give you a ‘banana bag’—it has vitamins and electrolytes. You’ve been on pantoprazole and sucralfate at home—we’ll continue those, but through IV for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. I’ve been worried about not getting enough nutrition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We understand. Right now, we’re supporting you with fluids. We’re planning an upper endoscopy in the next day or two to look at your stomach pouch and the bypass connections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that be uncomfortable?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under sedation, so you’ll be asleep. It’s very safe. We’ll use it to check for ulcers or inflammation and treat anything we see."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2170-06-11 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m okay with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs from this morning look stable. White count is a bit low but not concerning. Your electrolytes are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel a little better today—still some nausea, but not as bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s encouraging. We’re going to try advancing your diet today—start with a stage 4 bariatric diet. Small portions, soft foods."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like what?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Things like mashed potatoes, scrambled eggs, pureed soups. Easy to digest. We’ll watch you after the first meal to make sure you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2170-06-12 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can try that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with lunch—no heaving, and you said the food stayed down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I only had a small amount, but it felt okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll keep you on the IV protonix twice a day for acid suppression. The endoscopy is scheduled for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there a chance they’ll find another ulcer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. Given your history, we’re especially looking at the anastomosis and the gastric pouch. If we see an ulcer, we can treat it with medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if it’s bad, could I need another G-tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. Most of these can be managed with meds and diet. We’re not planning any tubes unless absolutely necessary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2170-06-12 14:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, that’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from the endoscopy. You did great. The report shows your bypass anatomy looks good. No issues in the small intestine or connections."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. But… there was something, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, a small erosion was seen in the top part of your stomach remnant—the cardia. It’s not a full ulcer, but it’s irritated and likely causing your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can that heal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. We’ll keep you on high-dose pantoprazole twice a day and sucralfate four times a day. Those help protect and heal the lining."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2170-06-13 13:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll advance you to a stage 5 bariatric diet—regular soft foods, but still small portions. No spicy or acidic foods for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Vital signs are stable, you’re tolerating food, and your pain is controlled. We’re going to discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I be on at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue sucralfate four times a day, pantoprazole twice daily, and metoclopramide as needed for nausea. We’re adjusting your citalopram and aripiprazole doses too—lower now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll see your surgeon in one week. Call us sooner if you have chest pain, vomiting, black stools, fever, or worsening pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No lifting, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct—nothing over 10 pounds until your follow-up. And avoid driving while on pain meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thank you for helping me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2170-06-14 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep resting, stay hydrated, and we’ll see you soon in clinic."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2170-06-11 21:16:00",
    "admission_end": "2170-06-14 10:38:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for worsening dry heaves and abdominal pain following removal of her G-tube, with a history of gastric bypass and anastomotic ulcers. She was hydrated with IV fluids and started on IV proton pump inhibition. By hospital day 2, she tolerated a stage 4 bariatric diet. An upper endoscopy on day 3 revealed a small erosion in the gastric remnant cardia, with otherwise normal findings. She progressed to a stage 5 diet, remained stable, and was discharged home on oral pantoprazole and sucralfate with instructions for follow-up. Her symptoms improved with medical management, and no surgical intervention was required.",
    "problems": [
      "Other complications of other bariatric procedure",
      "Other specified procedures as the cause of abnormal reaction of patient, or of later complication, without mention of misadventure at time of procedure",
      "Esophageal reflux"
    ]
  }
}
